    "manual_sample": "717 manually reviewed candidates from40 source documents,20 EUR-Lex and20 UN. Each version judged on its own candidate bank.",
    "manually_good_pair": "question_rating >=4 out of5 and answer_status is ok or minor, not major. This is an intrinsic-quality proxy, not mode/metadata compliance.",
    "native_acceptance": "Completed numeric total, quality_audit_status clear or minor_issues; for UN also faith_grounding >=3. Diagnostic acceptance rule, not a claim of actual delivered output.",
    "ranking": "Exported candidate_rank=1 is highest combined native faithfulness/quality total. It does not incorporate the acceptance gate. Ranking comparison uses82 document/mode families where all three versions generated candidates; ties at manual maximum count as hits.",
    "best_valid": "Best manual question score among candidates whose manually assessed answer has no major defect. Highest-scored native candidate must also have no major answer defect to count as a hit.",
    "limitations": [
      "No controlled fixed-candidate-bank comparison of all three verifier prompts was run. Across all1778 candidates, exact whitespace-normalized QA overlap is only1 original/revised pair and1 revised/simple pair; none across all three.",
      "Generation quality, number of candidates, mode policies, metadata validity, and candidate difficulty differ by version. Descriptive rates cannot isolate verifier accuracy improvements.",
      "Manual judgments are agent ratings rather than human gold labels; only40of100 documents reviewed.",
      "Good intrinsic questions may legitimately fail intended mode or metadata requirements; withheld does not automatically mean an erroneous rejection.",
      "Highest native total includes answer faithfulness, while primary manual ranking measures question quality. Answer-aware ranking is supplied separately."
    ]
